# scaling.vrs: scaling D20 (Session 1), one player in game. sc-wave (tools/vrclient/fixtures/sc-wave.json: wave 1 of 4
# CHAR_Bandit_Thug -301730941, wave 2 of 4 thugs with the boss CHAR_Bandit_Foreman_VBlood 2122229952 (prefab level 20,
# Reference Data/unit_index.tsv), scaling unitsPerPlayer 2, levelFromPlayers true, levelOffset 2, levelPerWave 1) at sc-a.
# Part A (IncludeAdmins true): Chaos counts, so wave 1 logs "players 1, gear <g>, level <g+2>, units 4 -> 4" (one player
# adds nothing) and its thugs stand at level g+2; wave 2 (after `.devkill` of wave 1) logs level g+3, its thugs at g+3 and
# the V Blood at its own level 20. `.nyar event info sc-wave` shows both scaling lines; a set out of range replies D1's
# reason. Part B is run separately with IncludeAdmins false (--var PART=B is not a branch: run scaling-admins-off.vrs).
#
# Needs: a Release DLL with scaling step 3; sc-wave (fixture above) enabled, every other spawning definition disabled;
# [Scoreboard] IncludeAdmins = true; NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devgear, .devkill) and DevChatEcho; no purge cooldown; Chaos
# invulnerable (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false).
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
mark
chat .devgear
expect-log \[DEV GEAR\] armor=[0-9.]+ spell=[0-9.]+ weapon=[0-9.]+ sum=[0-9.]+ full=[0-9.]+ floor=(?P<G>[0-9]+)
calc L1 = ${G} + 2
calc L2 = ${G} + 3
chat .nyar event info sc-wave
expect-reply scaling: +2 units a player beyond the first, level players' gear +2, +1 a wave
mark
chat .nyar event start sc-wave
expect-log event sc-wave started by manual timeout=20
expect-log event sc-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling sc-wave wave 1: players 1, gear ${G}, level ${L1}, units 4 -> 4
wait 8
chat .nyar debug here 40
expect-log CHAR_Bandit_Thug sc-wave left [0-9]+s lvl ${L1}
chat .nyar event info sc-wave
expect-reply scaling now: 1 players, gear ${G}, level ${L1}
shot full sc-info-running
# wave 2: wave 1 killed, the boss keeps its own level
chat .devkill -301730941 40
expect-log \[DEV KILL\] n=4
expect-log event sc-wave wave 2/2 timeout=60
expect-seen \[nyar\] scaling sc-wave wave 2: players 1, gear ${G}, level ${L2}, units 5 -> 5
wait 8
chat .nyar debug here 40
expect-log CHAR_Bandit_Thug sc-wave left [0-9]+s lvl ${L2}
expect-seen CHAR_Bandit_Foreman_VBlood sc-wave left [0-9]+s lvl 20
shot full sc-wave2
# a value out of range: D1's reason in real chat
chat .nyar event set sc-wave action.scaling.unitsPerPlayer 6
expect-reply action.scaling.unitsPerPlayer must be 0-5
shot full sc-set-refused
chat .nyar event stop sc-wave
expect-log event sc-wave stopped
chat .nyar event info sc-wave
expect-no-log scaling now: timeout=5
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
console TPHome
wait 3
